    <Namespace structures:ref="biom" xsi:nil="true"/>
    <DocumentationText>A number assigned to the tier level of a particular face image feature point</DocumentationText>
    <SubPropertyOf structures:ref="biom.FaceImageFeaturePointTierAbstract" xsi:nil="true"/>
    <Datatype structures:ref="biom.FaceImageFeaturePointTierCodeType" xsi:nil="true"/>
  </DataProperty>
  <DataProperty structures:id="biom.FaceImageFeaturePointTierNumeric">
    <Name>FaceImageFeaturePointTierNumeric</Name>
    <Namespace structures:ref="biom" xsi:nil="true"/>
    <DocumentationText>A user-defined number assigned to the tier level of a particular face image feature point</DocumentationText>
    <SubPropertyOf structures:ref="biom.FaceImageFeaturePointTierAbstract" xsi:nil="true"/>
    <Datatype structures:ref="biom.FaceImageFeaturePointTierNumericType" xsi:nil="true"/>
  </DataProperty>
  <DataProperty structures:id="biom.FaceImageLightingArtifactsCode">
    <Name>FaceImageLightingArtifactsCode</Name>
    <Namespace structures:ref="biom" xsi:nil="true"/>
    <DocumentationText>A lighting artifact in this face image</DocumentationText>
    <Datatype structures:ref="biom.FaceImageLightingArtifactsCodeType" xsi:nil="true"/>
  </DataProperty>
  <ObjectProperty structures:id="biom.FaceImageOcclusion">
    <Name>FaceImageOcclusion</Name>
    <Namespace structures:ref="biom" xsi:nil="true"/>
    <DocumentationText>A blockage in a face image</DocumentationText>
    <Class structures:ref="biom.FaceImageOcclusionType" xsi:nil="true"/>
  </ObjectProperty>
  <DataProperty structures:id="biom.FaceImageOcclusionCategoryCode">
    <Name>FaceImageOcclusionCategoryCode</Name>
    <Namespace structures:ref="biom" xsi:nil="true"/>
    <DocumentationText>A kind of a blockage in a face image</DocumentationText>
    <Datatype structures:ref="biom.ImageOcclusionCategoryCodeType" xsi:nil="true"/>
  </DataProperty>
  <DataProperty structures:id="biom.FaceImageOcclusionOpacityCode">
    <Name>FaceImageOcclusionOpacityCode</Name>
    <Namespace structures:ref="biom" xsi:nil="true"/>
    <DocumentationText>A level of opacity of a blockage in this face image</DocumentationText>
    <Datatype structures:ref="biom.ImageOcclusionOpacityCodeType" xsi:nil="true"/>
  </DataProperty>
  <DataProperty structures:id="biom.FaceImagePoseOffsetAngleMeasure">
    <Name>FaceImagePoseOffsetAngleMeasure</Name>
    <Namespace structures:ref="biom" xsi:nil="true"/>
    <DocumentationText>An angular offset of a subject from full face or a profile, for an angled pose</DocumentationText>
    <Datatype structures:ref="xs.integer" xsi:nil="true"/>
  </DataProperty>
  <ObjectProperty structures:id="biom.FaceImageSubjectPoseAbstract">
    <Name>FaceImageSubjectPoseAbstract</Name>
    <Namespace structures:ref="biom" xsi:nil="true"/>
    <DocumentationText>A data concept for a pose of a subject</DocumentationText>
    <AbstractIndicator>true</AbstractIndicator>
  </ObjectProperty>
  <DataProperty structures:id="biom.FaceImageSubjectPoseCode">
    <Name>FaceImageSubjectPoseCode</Name>
    <Namespace structures:ref="biom" xsi:nil="true"/>
    <DocumentationText>A pose of a subject</DocumentationText>
    <SubPropertyOf structures:ref="biom.FaceImageSubjectPoseAbstract" xsi:nil="true"/>
    <Datatype structures:ref="biom.SubjectPoseCodeType" xsi:nil="true"/>
  </DataProperty>
  <DataProperty structures:id="biom.FamiliarityValue">
    <Name>FamiliarityValue</Name>
    <Namespace structures:ref="biom" xsi:nil="true"/>
    <DocumentationText>An indication for the degree of familiarity between the data subject and the interlocutor.</DocumentationText>
    <Datatype structures:ref="biom.Integer0To5Type" xsi:nil="true"/>
  </DataProperty>
  <DataProperty structures:id="biom.FeatureColorCommentText">
    <Name>FeatureColorCommentText</Name>
    <Namespace structures:ref="biom" xsi:nil="true"/>
    <DocumentationText>A fourth information item, feature _ comment / COM, allows a free text comment or description to be provided by the examiner about the referenced field and subfield in this instance of a Type-9 record.</DocumentationText>
    <Datatype structures:ref="nc.TextType" xsi:nil="true"/>
  </DataProperty>
  <DataProperty structures:id="biom.FeatureColorFieldOccurenceReferencedValue">
    <Name>FeatureColorFieldOccurenceReferencedValue</Name>
    <Namespace structures:ref="biom" xsi:nil="true"/>
    <DocumentationText>A second information item, feature _ field occurrence / FTO, indicates which repeating subfield of the specified field the label is applied to. Note that this is a 1-based index, not a 0-based index. Occurrences are numbered starting with 1.</DocumentationText>
    <Datatype structures:ref="xs.positiveInteger" xsi:nil="true"/>
  </DataProperty>
  <DataProperty structures:id="biom.FeatureColorFieldReferencedCode">
    <Name>FeatureColorFieldReferencedCode</Name>
    <Namespace structures:ref="biom" xsi:nil="true"/>
    <DocumentationText>A data for one or both of the third or fourth information items shall be present in each subfield. The first two information items are mandatory. The first information item, feature - field number / FTF, indicates the field which is annotated with c</DocumentationText>
    <Datatype structures:ref="biom.EFSFieldNumberCodeType" xsi:nil="true"/>
  </DataProperty>
  <DataProperty structures:id="biom.FeatureColorHexidecimalValue">
    <Name>FeatureColorHexidecimalValue</Name>
    <Namespace structures:ref="biom" xsi:nil="true"/>
    <DocumentationText>A third information item, feature _ color / FTC, is an RGB color value expressed as a hexadecimal number.Some basic colors are red (FF0000), yellow (FFFF00), blue (0000FF), green (008000), black (000000) and white (FFFFFF). Leading zeros are require</DocumentationText>
    <Datatype structures:ref="xs.hexBinary" xsi:nil="true"/>
  </DataProperty>
  <DataProperty structures:id="biom.FeatureLabelID">
    <Name>FeatureLabelID</Name>
    <Namespace structures:ref="biom" xsi:nil="true"/>
    <DocumentationText>An index identifier or unique label applied to minutiae by a latent examiner to allow correlation of features between images</DocumentationText>
    <Datatype structures:ref="nc.TextType" xsi:nil="true"/>
  </DataProperty>
  <DataProperty structures:id="biom.FeatureLineColorValue">
    <Name>FeatureLineColorValue</Name>
    <Namespace structures:ref="biom" xsi:nil="true"/>
    <DocumentationText>A fifth information item, line color / TLC, is an RGB color value expressed as a hexadecimal number. Some basic colors are red (FF0000), yellow (FFFF00), blue (0000FF), green (008000), black (000000) and white (FFFFFF). Leading zeros are required.</DocumentationText>
    <Datatype structures:ref="xs.hexBinary" xsi:nil="true"/>
  </DataProperty>
  <DataProperty structures:id="biom.FeatureLineThicknessValue">
    <Name>FeatureLineThicknessValue</Name>
    <Namespace structures:ref="biom" xsi:nil="true"/>
    <DocumentationText>A sixth information item, line thickness / TLT, is expressed as a positive integer. Thickness is expressed in units of 0.01 mm Any value from 1 through 99 is acceptable; suggested values are 3 (thin); 6 (medium); 9 (thick), and 15 (bold).</DocumentationText>
    <Datatype structures:ref="biom.Integer1to99Type" xsi:nil="true"/>
  </DataProperty>
  <ObjectProperty structures:id="biom.FeaturePointCategoryAbstract">
    <Name>FeaturePointCategoryAbstract</Name>
    <Namespace structures:ref="biom" xsi:nil="true"/>
    <DocumentationText>A data concept for a kind of feature point of a captured facial image</DocumentationText>
    <AbstractIndicator>true</AbstractIndicator>
  </ObjectProperty>
  <DataProperty structures:id="biom.FeaturePointCategoryCode">
    <Name>FeaturePointCategoryCode</Name>
    <Namespace structures:ref="biom" xsi:nil="true"/>
